<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="Pawn" inherits="Node" api_type="extension" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot/master/doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		Makes its parent possessable: the framework's half of a playable thing.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Add it as a child of the node a player drives. It is a child rather than the root because the root is whatever the game needs - a [CharacterBody3D], an [Area2D], a [RigidBody3D] - and that choice belongs to the game; everything here works on [method get_pawn_root].
		Override [code]_setup_input_component[/code] to bind actions, [code]_possessed[/code] and [code]_unpossessed[/code] to react to a controller taking it over. [method add_movement_input] and [method consume_movement_input_vector] keep "what the player asked for" separate from how the pawn moves.
		In a networked game the server drives the pawn and [member replicate_transform] mirrors where it ended up; guard movement with [method has_authority] so the same script is correct in every net mode. [method get_local_role] says what this copy is: [constant World.ROLE_AUTHORITY], [constant World.ROLE_AUTONOMOUS_PROXY] for the player driving it, or [constant World.ROLE_SIMULATED_PROXY] for everyone else.
	</description>
